  "releaseNotes": "## 2.0.4 - 2026-11-10\n\n- Restores existing conversations when switching models with Codex or OpenCode, including when the native session can no longer resume. Keeps Agent instructions and approvals, and uses authorized models for history recovery.\n- Uses the selected model's configured output budget for the first structured API extraction. If the upstream reports an output-token limit, retries with a larger budget within the available context and upstream limits, without extending the request timeout.\n- Preserves upstream truncation signals even when a Responses model exhausts its budget before returning visible text.\n- Reuses the verified Runtime 1.0.0 and existing sandbox templates. No configuration or conversation migration is required.",
